{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall be holy</b> — above it is written 'and you shall keep My charge,' and juxtaposed to it is 'holy you shall be' — that if he guards himself from sin, sin no longer comes upon him, and they sanctify him from above." "<b>I am YHWH your Elohim</b> — and juxtaposed to it is 'Speak to all the congregation of the children of Israel' — to say that the children of Israel crown HaShem and declare YHWH one." "<b>Congregation of the children of Israel</b> — and juxtaposed to it is 'holy' — for a matter of holiness requires ten, which is a congregation. And so YHWH your Elohim appears five times in this passage. 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — 'You shall revere every man his mother and his father' — to say that the honor of father and mother and their reverence is weighed equally against the honor of HaShem and His reverence. And juxtaposed to it is 'you shall keep My Sabbaths' — that if his father says to him to profane the Sabbath, he shall not listen to him. And juxtaposed to Sabbath is idolatry, for they are weighed equally — one who libates wine to idolatry and one who profanes the Sabbath, as stated in the first chapter of Ḥullin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:55.066305191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}